# File: tests/blender/test_geometry_normals.py
# Generated from: specs/144-fix-geometry-normals-rejecting-correctly-facing-open-surfaces-on-environment-pieces/requirements.md
Feature: geometry.normals judges open sheets by winding and closed parts by orientation

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A correctly facing single open quad passes wherever it sits
    Given one planar quad, axis-aligned or tilted, placed anywhere relative to the origin
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then no geometry.normals finding is reported for any placement

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A consistently wound open sheet passes regardless of which way it faces
    Given a floor and back wall facing into a room, or a welded grid ground sheet
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then no geometry.normals finding is reported

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Inconsistent winding inside an open sheet is still reported
    Given an open sheet with one face wound opposite to its neighbours
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then a geometry.normals finding counts that face

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Closed islands are still required to face outward
    Given a closed box with one flipped face, or a box turned inside out
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then a geometry.normals finding is reported as before

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Islands are judged independently
    Given one mesh with a correct box, a floor quad, and a box with one flipped face
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then the geometry.normals finding counts exactly the one flipped face

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Welded touching closed primitives pass
    Given two correct boxes touching at a vertex, an edge, or part of a face, merged by distance
    When the geometry checks run on it
    Then no geometry.normals finding is reported

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Remediation text fits open surfaces
    Given a geometry.normals finding
    When the report is produced
    Then the remediation distinguishes closed parts facing outward from open sheets wound consistently

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: The authoring rule is documented
    Given the asset contract and the model-asset skill documents
    When an author building an environment piece reads them
    Then they state the open-sheet, closed-part, and touching-primitive rules the validator applies
